WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.067 --> 00:00:02.701
-While the Biden administration

00:00:02.701 --> 00:00:03.934
is doing everything possible

00:00:03.934 --> 00:00:05.701
to counter Russia's invasion
of Ukraine,

00:00:05.701 --> 00:00:08.200
while avoiding a direct
military confrontation

00:00:08.200 --> 00:00:10.567
that could spiral
out of control,

00:00:10.567 --> 00:00:12.267
Republicans
and right-wing pundits

00:00:12.267 --> 00:00:14.767
are pitching
increasingly reckless ideas

00:00:14.767 --> 00:00:17.067
that would drastically
escalate the conflict.

00:00:17.067 --> 00:00:19.901
Oh, and Donald Trump
is blaming it on windmills.

00:00:19.901 --> 00:00:21.801
[ Laughter ]
For more on this,
it's time for "A Closer Look."

00:00:21.801 --> 00:00:26.467
♪♪
[ Cheering and applause ]

00:00:26.467 --> 00:00:29.367
Russia's brutal and illegal
invasion of Ukraine

00:00:29.367 --> 00:00:31.667
set off a dire
humanitarian crisis

00:00:31.667 --> 00:00:34.400
and united virtually
the entire world in opposition.

00:00:34.400 --> 00:00:36.067
Even fast food chains

00:00:36.067 --> 00:00:37.934
are pulling their business
from Russia.

00:00:37.934 --> 00:00:40.067
-Several more big-name
companies announced

00:00:40.067 --> 00:00:43.200
they're ending at least part
of their operations in Russia.

00:00:43.200 --> 00:00:45.234
McDonald's, Starbucks,
Coca-Cola,

00:00:45.234 --> 00:00:48.367
Pepsi, KFC, Pizza Hut,
and Unilever

00:00:48.367 --> 00:00:50.601
are scaling back
or ending their sales

00:00:50.601 --> 00:00:52.133
of their product in Russia.

00:00:52.133 --> 00:00:53.534
-Even Pizza Hut!

00:00:53.534 --> 00:00:57.167
Putin tried to outpizza the Hut,
but he learned the hard way,

00:00:57.167 --> 00:00:59.667
in Russia, Hut outpizzas you.

00:00:59.667 --> 00:01:01.067
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:01:01.067 --> 00:01:03.467
And KFC, too.
KFC, too.

00:01:03.467 --> 00:01:05.801
What a bummer for the
Russian Colonel Sanders,

00:01:05.801 --> 00:01:06.934
or, as he's known in Russia...

00:01:09.634 --> 00:01:12.534
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:01:12.534 --> 00:01:15.334
So Russia lost its Pizza Hut
and KFCs

00:01:15.334 --> 00:01:17.267
and, as a form
of further punishment,

00:01:17.267 --> 00:01:20.467
a Sbarro's in Red Square
just opened.

00:01:20.467 --> 00:01:23.033
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:01:23.033 --> 00:01:24.100
There are no good outcomes

00:01:24.100 --> 00:01:25.300
for anyone here,
including Russia.

00:01:25.300 --> 00:01:27.067
The regime is
under intense sanctions

00:01:27.067 --> 00:01:29.033
or, in the case of the Sbarro,
sbanctions,

00:01:29.033 --> 00:01:32.167
[ Laughter ]
and facing nearly universal
global condemnation

00:01:32.167 --> 00:01:33.534
and, on top of that,
they're encountering

00:01:33.534 --> 00:01:35.601
brave resistance
from the Ukrainian people

00:01:35.601 --> 00:01:37.734
and their president,
Volodymyr Zelenskyy,

00:01:37.734 --> 00:01:39.200
who said,
in a new interview this week,

00:01:39.200 --> 00:01:41.767
that this war can only end
with dialogue.

00:01:41.767 --> 00:01:44.200
-Can you make a compromise
with Putin?

00:01:44.200 --> 00:01:46.367
Can you trust Putin?

00:01:46.367 --> 00:01:47.767
-Trust?

00:01:47.767 --> 00:01:48.501
Oh, no.

00:01:48.501 --> 00:01:50.968
I trust only my family.

00:01:50.968 --> 00:01:52.334
-How can you make a deal

00:01:52.334 --> 00:01:54.367
with somebody
you don't trust, then?

00:01:54.367 --> 00:01:56.334
-We have to.
We have to.

00:01:56.334 --> 00:02:00.267
Because, to stop this war,
how to stop this war?

00:02:00.267 --> 00:02:01.300
Only dialogue.

00:02:01.300 --> 00:02:03.968
-What would be your message

00:02:03.968 --> 00:02:06.334
to President Vladimir Putin
right now?

00:02:06.334 --> 00:02:07.767
-Right now?

00:02:07.767 --> 00:02:10.801
Right now, stop the war,
begin to speak. That's it.

00:02:10.801 --> 00:02:12.801
--And what if he doesn't?

00:02:12.801 --> 00:02:14.567
-I think he will.

00:02:14.567 --> 00:02:15.801
I think he will.

00:02:15.801 --> 00:02:17.901
I think he sees
that we're strong.

00:02:17.901 --> 00:02:18.667
He will.

00:02:18.667 --> 00:02:19.834
-That's really incredible.

00:02:19.834 --> 00:02:21.267
Even a guy who is being hunted

00:02:21.267 --> 00:02:23.400
by one of the world's
most barbaric autocrats

00:02:23.400 --> 00:02:24.834
still believes
in the power of dialogue.

00:02:24.834 --> 00:02:26.400
And let's not forget --
this guy,

00:02:26.400 --> 00:02:28.133
who is now courageously
leading his people

00:02:28.133 --> 00:02:29.367
in defense of their homeland

00:02:29.367 --> 00:02:31.734
was once Ukraine's top comedian,

00:02:31.734 --> 00:02:33.267
[ Laughter ]
which makes it
even more incredible

00:02:33.267 --> 00:02:37.100
because the comedians I know
do not believe in dialogue.

00:02:37.100 --> 00:02:38.634
They believe in monologue.

00:02:38.634 --> 00:02:39.767
[ Laughter ]
Every conversation

00:02:39.767 --> 00:02:40.968
between my comedian friends

00:02:40.968 --> 00:02:43.334
is just two people performing
at each other.

00:02:43.334 --> 00:02:46.000
[ Laughter ]
And you know when one of them
says something funny

00:02:46.000 --> 00:02:48.300
because the other one says,

00:02:48.300 --> 00:02:49.367
"That's funny."

00:02:49.367 --> 00:02:51.367
[ Laughter ]

00:02:51.367 --> 00:02:52.801
Also, can we go back to this?

00:02:52.801 --> 00:02:54.868
-Can you trust Putin?

00:02:54.868 --> 00:02:56.267
-Trust?

00:02:56.267 --> 00:02:59.000
Oh, no.
I trust only my family.

00:02:59.000 --> 00:03:00.667
-I mean, that's even
more impressive to me

00:03:00.667 --> 00:03:03.167
because I don't trust my family,
even a little bit.

00:03:03.167 --> 00:03:04.767
[ Laughter ]

00:03:04.767 --> 00:03:05.901
Especially my kids.

00:03:05.901 --> 00:03:07.334
Couple of nights ago --
true story --

00:03:07.334 --> 00:03:09.567
our oldest threw up,
so we brought him in bed with us

00:03:09.567 --> 00:03:11.300
and we got him a bowl,
in case it happened again.

00:03:11.300 --> 00:03:12.968
Twenty minutes later,
the three-year-old

00:03:12.968 --> 00:03:14.601
started screaming
that he's also going to puke

00:03:14.601 --> 00:03:16.067
and I said,
"I think you're faking it

00:03:16.067 --> 00:03:17.767
and I think you just want
to get in bed with us, too."

00:03:17.767 --> 00:03:19.701
And he said,
"No, I'm really, really sick."

00:03:19.701 --> 00:03:21.667
So we got in bed,
he got his own bowl,

00:03:21.667 --> 00:03:23.601
and tell me,
based on this photo,

00:03:23.601 --> 00:03:25.367
if you think
he was telling the truth.

00:03:25.367 --> 00:03:28.234
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:03:31.067 --> 00:03:34.067
So, while I know it can't be
easy to talk to Putin,

00:03:34.067 --> 00:03:35.534
at least you don't have
to negotiate

00:03:35.534 --> 00:03:37.234
with Axel at 3:00 am.

00:03:37.234 --> 00:03:39.000
[ Laughter ]
The point is,

00:03:39.000 --> 00:03:41.834
if even Zelenskyy still believes
in the power of dialogue,

00:03:41.834 --> 00:03:43.767
then the rest of us should, too,
because he's right --

00:03:43.767 --> 00:03:46.701
that's the only way
this horrific conflict can end.

00:03:46.701 --> 00:03:48.767
Reckless escalation
will only make things worse,

00:03:48.767 --> 00:03:52.133
which is why irresponsible
GOP politicians and pundits need

00:03:52.133 --> 00:03:54.400
to stop floating crazy ideas

00:03:54.400 --> 00:03:56.834
that would only heighten tension
between nuclear powers.

00:03:56.834 --> 00:03:58.868
Like, for example, when we told
you earlier this week

00:03:58.868 --> 00:04:01.334
that Donald Trump
had come up with an insane idea

00:04:01.334 --> 00:04:04.601
to bomb Russia, but pretend
it was China that did it.

00:04:04.601 --> 00:04:06.901
-According to CBS,
Trump says we should,

00:04:06.901 --> 00:04:10.501
"Put the Chinese flag
on some F-22 fighter jets"

00:04:10.501 --> 00:04:13.400
and "bomb the [bleep]
out of Russia."

00:04:13.400 --> 00:04:15.267
[ Laughter ]
Now, Trump reportedly
made the suggestion

00:04:15.267 --> 00:04:19.467
to top GOP donors at a retreat
in New Orleans this weekend.

00:04:19.467 --> 00:04:22.234
The crowd apparently laughed
when he said this, so,

00:04:22.234 --> 00:04:24.300
let's just assume it was a joke.

00:04:24.300 --> 00:04:26.100
-No, let's not assume that.

00:04:26.100 --> 00:04:28.667
[ Laughter ]
I mean, a lot of us assumed
that he was joking

00:04:28.667 --> 00:04:30.234
when he said he was going
to run for president

00:04:30.234 --> 00:04:31.167
because, you know, he was

00:04:31.167 --> 00:04:33.300
a famously broke
game show idiot.

00:04:33.300 --> 00:04:35.667
[ Laughter ]
But Trump is always joking,
until he's not.

00:04:35.667 --> 00:04:37.434
He's like a husband
pitching a three-way

00:04:37.434 --> 00:04:38.601
to his wife and her best friend.

00:04:38.601 --> 00:04:40.701
[ Laughter ]
"I mean, that would be so funny,

00:04:40.701 --> 00:04:42.467
the three of us, right?

00:04:42.467 --> 00:04:44.400
Would it be funny?

00:04:44.400 --> 00:04:47.501
Should we do it, though,
as a joke?"

00:04:47.501 --> 00:04:48.467
[ Laughter ]

00:04:48.467 --> 00:04:50.100
That's how Trump
gauges reaction,

00:04:50.100 --> 00:04:51.667
by pretending he's not serious.

00:04:51.667 --> 00:04:55.000
Remember when he was supposedly
joking, in 2016,

00:04:55.000 --> 00:04:57.000
that Russia should hack
Hillary's emails

00:04:57.000 --> 00:04:58.567
and then they actually did it?

00:04:58.567 --> 00:05:01.801
Or when he looked one of his
science advisors dead in the eye

00:05:01.801 --> 00:05:03.467
and suggested
we should inject people

00:05:03.467 --> 00:05:05.534
with disinfectant
to cure coronavirus

00:05:05.534 --> 00:05:07.834
and then later claimed
he was joking?

00:05:07.834 --> 00:05:10.567
If that was a joke, then why
did her face look like that?

00:05:10.567 --> 00:05:11.501
[ Laughter ]

00:05:11.501 --> 00:05:12.701
She looks like she just heard

00:05:12.701 --> 00:05:14.400
they opened a Sbarro in D.C.

00:05:14.400 --> 00:05:16.033
[ Laughter ]

00:05:16.033 --> 00:05:18.400
That's what Trump does --
he floats crazy [bleep]

00:05:18.400 --> 00:05:19.767
and sees how far he can take it.

00:05:19.767 --> 00:05:22.534
If one idea gets rejected,
he just tries another one.

00:05:22.534 --> 00:05:23.801
[ As Trump ]
Alright, how about this?
Instead of putting

00:05:23.801 --> 00:05:24.901
the Chinese flag on the jets,

00:05:24.901 --> 00:05:26.601
we give them a fake nose
and a mustache.

00:05:26.601 --> 00:05:28.200
[ Laughter ]

00:05:28.200 --> 00:05:31.567
Or we stack three jets on top
of each other in a trench coat

00:05:31.567 --> 00:05:33.133
and pretend they're
a businessman.

00:05:33.133 --> 00:05:34.434
[ Laughter ]
Out-of-town businessman.

00:05:34.434 --> 00:05:36.267
It could work.
Would that work?

00:05:36.267 --> 00:05:38.300
Let's remember --
no one seriously thought

00:05:38.300 --> 00:05:40.200
Trump would stage a coup,
either,

00:05:40.200 --> 00:05:43.334
and then he ended up siccing
an angry mob of insurrectionists

00:05:43.334 --> 00:05:45.367
and werewolves on the Capitol.

00:05:45.367 --> 00:05:47.534
[ Laughter ]
Or how about Trump's obsession
with windmills?

00:05:47.534 --> 00:05:50.300
You might think that's all
a big joke, too, but it's not.

00:05:50.300 --> 00:05:51.734
He's still obsessed with them.

00:05:51.734 --> 00:05:54.701
In fact, this week, Trump was
asked about the Russian invasion

00:05:54.701 --> 00:05:56.567
and used it
as a jumping-off point

00:05:56.567 --> 00:05:59.267
to start ranting incoherently,
once again,

00:05:59.267 --> 00:06:01.133
about how much
he hates windmills.

00:06:01.133 --> 00:06:02.834
-What do you see happening
next, then?

00:06:02.834 --> 00:06:04.601
Because it seems like
the tensions are high.

00:06:04.601 --> 00:06:05.701
How does this all end?

00:06:05.701 --> 00:06:07.300
Is this going to be like
a long-term thing?

00:06:07.300 --> 00:06:09.200
How do you see it unfolding?
-Well -- and I said this

00:06:09.200 --> 00:06:14.100
a long time ago --
if this happens, we are

00:06:14.100 --> 00:06:16.901
playing right into the hands
of green energy.

00:06:16.901 --> 00:06:19.267
The windmills, they don't work.

00:06:19.267 --> 00:06:20.067
[ Laughter ]
They're too expensive.

00:06:20.067 --> 00:06:20.968
They kill all the birds.

00:06:20.968 --> 00:06:22.133
They ruin your landscapes.

00:06:22.133 --> 00:06:23.334
[ Laughter ]
And yet, the environmentalists

00:06:23.334 --> 00:06:24.567
love the windmills.

00:06:24.567 --> 00:06:26.767
And I've been preaching this
for years.

00:06:26.767 --> 00:06:29.467
The windmills.
And I had them way down,

00:06:29.467 --> 00:06:31.667
but the windmills
are the most expensive energy

00:06:31.667 --> 00:06:34.167
you can have
and they don't work.

00:06:34.167 --> 00:06:36.400
And, by the way,
they last a period of ten years

00:06:36.400 --> 00:06:38.300
and, by the time
they start rusting and rotting

00:06:38.300 --> 00:06:40.734
all over the place,
nobody ever takes them down.

00:06:40.734 --> 00:06:43.934
They just go on to the next
piece of prairie or land

00:06:43.934 --> 00:06:45.267
and destroy that.

00:06:45.267 --> 00:06:47.901
-First of all, I feel like you
should like windmills

00:06:47.901 --> 00:06:50.467
because you both just go
in [bleep] circles all the time

00:06:50.467 --> 00:06:52.100
[ Laughter ]
and make a giant sucking sound.

00:06:52.100 --> 00:06:53.767
I mean, seriously,
how does he get

00:06:53.767 --> 00:06:55.400
from Russia's invasion
of Ukraine

00:06:55.400 --> 00:06:57.167
to windmills in one sentence?

00:06:57.167 --> 00:06:58.300
[ Laughter ]

00:06:58.300 --> 00:07:01.434
Trump's favorite game is
One Degree of Windmills.

00:07:01.434 --> 00:07:04.400
[ As Trump ]
Give me any topic and I'll tie
it to windmills in one move.

00:07:04.400 --> 00:07:06.300
"Uh, I don't know.

00:07:06.300 --> 00:07:07.300
Inflation."

00:07:07.300 --> 00:07:08.334
[ As Trump ]
And, with inflation,

00:07:08.334 --> 00:07:10.033
people are paying twice,
maybe three times

00:07:10.033 --> 00:07:11.734
what they paid
for a windmill last year.

00:07:11.734 --> 00:07:13.033
[ Laughter ]
I'm really good at it.

00:07:13.033 --> 00:07:14.734
I'm really good
at One Degree of Windmills.

00:07:14.734 --> 00:07:15.834
[ Laughter ]

00:07:15.834 --> 00:07:17.534
This is the leader
of the Republican Party.

00:07:17.534 --> 00:07:19.601
He's their most likely nominee
in 2024

00:07:19.601 --> 00:07:20.801
and, whether he runs or not,

00:07:20.801 --> 00:07:22.968
he still wields tremendous power
over the party.

00:07:22.968 --> 00:07:25.234
Republicans are all desperate
to lavish praise on him

00:07:25.234 --> 00:07:26.667
and do whatever
he orders them to do.

00:07:26.667 --> 00:07:28.067
Even his supposed critics,

00:07:28.067 --> 00:07:29.934
like his former
Attorney General Bill Barr,

00:07:29.934 --> 00:07:31.367
who has a new sham book out

00:07:31.367 --> 00:07:33.467
supposedly criticizing
Trump's behavior

00:07:33.467 --> 00:07:35.400
and who said,
on Fox News this week,

00:07:35.400 --> 00:07:36.467
Trump is unhinged.

00:07:36.467 --> 00:07:38.300
-What do you think was
the most alarming

00:07:38.300 --> 00:07:42.901
or unsettling moment for you
in the administration?

00:07:42.901 --> 00:07:44.868
-It was certainly unsettling
when I went in

00:07:44.868 --> 00:07:50.968
to talk to the president
about the election and,

00:07:50.968 --> 00:07:53.334
you know,
he was livid and shaking

00:07:53.334 --> 00:07:57.968
and, you know,
showed a lot of temper

00:07:57.968 --> 00:07:59.834
and yelling.

00:07:59.834 --> 00:08:01.534
That was a little unsettling.

00:08:01.534 --> 00:08:03.767
But the other thing that was
actually unsettling is later,

00:08:03.767 --> 00:08:09.000
when I went in to actually give
him my letter of resignation,

00:08:09.000 --> 00:08:11.868
he started talking about how he
had actually won the election

00:08:11.868 --> 00:08:13.868
and how the machines were rigged

00:08:13.868 --> 00:08:16.534
and that he was actually going
to be there for another term

00:08:16.534 --> 00:08:19.100
and he was very confident
of that.

00:08:19.100 --> 00:08:24.467
And I just felt this showed
a detachment from reality

00:08:24.467 --> 00:08:26.167
that was stunning to me.

00:08:26.167 --> 00:08:27.567
-That's what's in your book?

00:08:27.567 --> 00:08:29.767
You know he didn't just say
that [bleep] to you, right?

00:08:29.767 --> 00:08:31.534
[ Laughter ]
He said it to all of us,

00:08:31.534 --> 00:08:32.968
all the time.

00:08:32.968 --> 00:08:35.033
Wait, are we all supposed
to be writing books?

00:08:35.033 --> 00:08:37.300
[ Laughter ]
Am I going to walk
into Barnes &amp; Noble

00:08:37.300 --> 00:08:39.534
and see a tell-all
from my neighbor Bob?

00:08:39.534 --> 00:08:41.834
[ Laughter ]

00:08:41.834 --> 00:08:43.934
And also, you were stunned,
really?

00:08:43.934 --> 00:08:46.267
That's the moment
it finally sunk in for you

00:08:46.267 --> 00:08:49.100
that maybe this guy was
a little off, right at the end?

00:08:49.100 --> 00:08:51.033
[ Laughter ]
You're like a person who stopped
watching "Game of Thrones"

00:08:51.033 --> 00:08:53.767
because it was too violent
in the second-to-last episode.

00:08:53.767 --> 00:08:55.868
"I don't know, when The Hound
was fighting The Mountain,

00:08:55.868 --> 00:08:57.000
I just thought,
'That's enough for me.'"

00:08:57.000 --> 00:08:58.300
[ Laughter ]

00:08:58.300 --> 00:08:59.634
But just to illustrate the point

00:08:59.634 --> 00:09:02.300
that Trump is still very much
the leader of the GOP,

00:09:02.300 --> 00:09:04.167
even Barr,
who is now trying to cash in

00:09:04.167 --> 00:09:05.467
with a [bleep] tell-all,

00:09:05.467 --> 00:09:07.501
said, in an interview this week,
that, despite Trump's

00:09:07.501 --> 00:09:10.167
supposedly stunning detachment
from reality,

00:09:10.167 --> 00:09:13.601
he'd still vote for Trump
over a Democrat in 2024.

00:09:13.601 --> 00:09:17.400
-If he is the nominee
and your choice is

00:09:17.400 --> 00:09:19.567
Donald Trump or whoever's
running on the Democratic side,

00:09:19.567 --> 00:09:21.968
would you vote for him?

00:09:21.968 --> 00:09:24.567
-Because I believe that the
greatest threat to the country

00:09:24.567 --> 00:09:27.934
is the progressive agenda being
pushed by the Democratic Party,

00:09:27.934 --> 00:09:29.501
it's inconceivable to me

00:09:29.501 --> 00:09:31.534
that I wouldn't vote
for the Republican nominee.

00:09:31.534 --> 00:09:34.534
-So, even if he lied
about the election

00:09:34.534 --> 00:09:37.334
and threatened democracy,
as you write in your book,

00:09:37.334 --> 00:09:38.567
better than a Democrat?

00:09:38.567 --> 00:09:40.634
-It's hard to project
what the facts are going

00:09:40.634 --> 00:09:42.234
to turn out to be
three years hence,

00:09:42.234 --> 00:09:45.100
but as of now,
it's hard for me to conceive

00:09:45.100 --> 00:09:47.367
that I wouldn't vote
for the Republican nominee.

00:09:47.367 --> 00:09:49.634
-So then, why should we care
about anything you have to say?

00:09:49.634 --> 00:09:51.000
Trump's detached from reality,

00:09:51.000 --> 00:09:52.868
but you'd still support him
for president?

00:09:52.868 --> 00:09:55.167
You're like a cop who gets
a fax from the Zodiac Killer

00:09:55.167 --> 00:09:56.300
and says, "This guy's a sicko,

00:09:56.300 --> 00:09:57.701
but he'd be
a great math teacher."

00:09:57.701 --> 00:09:59.400
[ Laughter ]

00:09:59.400 --> 00:10:01.634
Interviewing this charlatan
is such a waste of air time.

00:10:01.634 --> 00:10:03.300
Don't help him plug
his dumb book.

00:10:03.300 --> 00:10:04.734
There are any number
of other books

00:10:04.734 --> 00:10:06.868
that deserve more attention.
If I had a book,

00:10:06.868 --> 00:10:07.901
that'd be a better use
of your time.

00:10:07.901 --> 00:10:09.467
Oh, wait, I do.
I have a brand-new

00:10:09.467 --> 00:10:10.400
children's book called...

00:10:11.767 --> 00:10:13.834
[ Laughter ]
My son Axel said it was great

00:10:13.834 --> 00:10:15.267
and it's not like he ever lies.

00:10:15.267 --> 00:10:17.801
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:10:17.801 --> 00:10:18.968
[ Bleep ]

00:10:18.968 --> 00:10:20.367
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:10:20.367 --> 00:10:22.734
On the one hand,
Biden is handling the situation

00:10:22.734 --> 00:10:24.267
very much how you'd hope
and expect --

00:10:24.267 --> 00:10:26.067
soberly and with restraint.

00:10:26.067 --> 00:10:27.667
On the other hand,
Trump and his supporters

00:10:27.667 --> 00:10:29.467
are just randomly
pitching crazy ideas

00:10:29.467 --> 00:10:32.534
for escalating the conflict,
like Fox host Jesse Watters,

00:10:32.534 --> 00:10:34.601
who had a retired
lieutenant general on his show

00:10:34.601 --> 00:10:37.167
and started just
spitballing reckless ideas

00:10:37.167 --> 00:10:39.767
for how other countries
could get involved militarily.

00:10:39.767 --> 00:10:42.234
-See if you think
this is a proper idea.

00:10:42.234 --> 00:10:46.200
What if we started
distracting the Russians

00:10:46.200 --> 00:10:47.200
and made them a little nervous?

00:10:47.200 --> 00:10:49.000
What if we had the Japanese

00:10:49.000 --> 00:10:51.267
stir up a little trouble
on their eastern flank?

00:10:51.267 --> 00:10:54.534
What if we sent some naval
assets into the Black Sea?

00:10:54.534 --> 00:10:56.834
Just say, "Hey, you know,
we're protecting Turkey,

00:10:56.834 --> 00:10:58.367
our NATO ally."
What if, you know,

00:10:58.367 --> 00:11:02.367
we scrambled a few jets
in the Baltics or something?

00:11:02.367 --> 00:11:05.334
Something to make the Russians,
maybe, think twice

00:11:05.334 --> 00:11:08.400
and take their eye off the ball
a little bit.

00:11:08.400 --> 00:11:10.067
-Do you think you're
in a pitch meeting

00:11:10.067 --> 00:11:11.734
for the new Steven Seagal movie?

00:11:11.734 --> 00:11:13.434
[ Laughter ]

00:11:13.434 --> 00:11:15.133
[ As Seagal ]
Tell me what you have, Jesse.

00:11:15.133 --> 00:11:17.834
[ As Watters ]
Eastern flank, scramble jets,

00:11:17.834 --> 00:11:20.100
naval assets,
stirred up trouble.

00:11:20.100 --> 00:11:21.234
[ As Seagal ]
That's very good, Jesse.

00:11:21.234 --> 00:11:22.801
[ Laughter ]

00:11:22.801 --> 00:11:24.534
The only problem is the budget
for this film

00:11:24.534 --> 00:11:26.133
is only $45.

00:11:26.133 --> 00:11:27.400
[ Laughter ]

00:11:27.400 --> 00:11:29.067
In what possible world
does anyone think

00:11:29.067 --> 00:11:31.734
the best path forward
with Vladimir Putin is

00:11:31.734 --> 00:11:33.501
to just [bleep] round with him?

00:11:33.501 --> 00:11:35.601
[ Laughter ]
If you have a rabid raccoon
in the corner of your garage,

00:11:35.601 --> 00:11:36.968
you call animal control,

00:11:36.968 --> 00:11:38.767
but I bet you could get someone
on Fox News to say --

00:11:38.767 --> 00:11:41.300
[ As Watters ]
"No! What you want to do is
set up a bunch of firecrackers

00:11:41.300 --> 00:11:42.701
to freak it out!
[ Laughter ]

00:11:42.701 --> 00:11:43.968
And then,
when it's all confused,

00:11:43.968 --> 00:11:46.067
you run in dressed
like a giant squirrel and say,

00:11:46.067 --> 00:11:47.801
'Come with me
if you want to live!'

00:11:47.801 --> 00:11:49.300
[ Laughter ]
And then, when it runs out,
surprise,

00:11:49.300 --> 00:11:51.801
you got a second rabid raccoon
you bought on the black market

00:11:51.801 --> 00:11:53.067
and now, they have to fight.

00:11:53.067 --> 00:11:54.834
Bang, boom, problem solved!

00:11:54.834 --> 00:11:56.200
[ Laughter ]

00:11:56.200 --> 00:11:58.801
Russia's invasion of Ukraine
is an unfathomable tragedy

00:11:58.801 --> 00:12:01.200
that has resulted
in a dire humanitarian crisis

00:12:01.200 --> 00:12:04.601
and what we need to do right now
to help the Ukrainian people is

00:12:04.601 --> 00:12:07.367
find a path forward toward
dialogue and de-escalation

00:12:07.367 --> 00:12:09.167
to end the conflict
as quickly as possible.

00:12:09.167 --> 00:12:10.901
What we don't need
are reckless ideas

00:12:10.901 --> 00:12:12.334
that would escalate
the conflict,

00:12:12.334 --> 00:12:14.434
from people who have no idea
what they're talking about,

00:12:14.434 --> 00:12:16.400
like former presidents
whose brains are...

00:12:16.400 --> 00:12:17.601
-Rusting and rotting.

00:12:17.601 --> 00:12:19.734
[ Laughter ]
-This has been "A Closer Look."

00:12:19.734 --> 00:12:23.667
♪♪

00:12:23.667 --> 00:12:25.133
God's Love We Deliver
cooks and brings

00:12:25.133 --> 00:12:26.634
